accTitle: Maven module layers and composition path
accDescr: The eleven Maven modules are grouped into five teaching layers: domain and simulator; application contracts and cognitive capabilities; graph runtime; durable PostgreSQL adapters; and application composition with evaluation support. The exact module names and project dependency details are listed in the adjacent chapter table and text. Arrows show the broad direction in which the application is assembled, not a deployment topology.
    Foundation["Business foundation<br/>Domain model and deterministic simulator"]
    Capabilities["Application and cognitive capabilities<br/>Core and memory · perception and grounding actions<br/>B1, B2, B3, B4, B6 services · planning strategies"]
    Runtime["Cognitive graph runtime<br/>LangGraph4j orchestration and LangChain4j adapters"]
    Persistence["Durable infrastructure adapters<br/>PostgreSQL stores and graph checkpoint adapter"]
    Application["Application composition<br/>Application graph and durable host"]
    Evaluation["Evaluation support<br/>Deterministic fixtures and test harnesses"]

    Foundation --> Capabilities
    Capabilities --> Runtime
    Runtime --> Persistence
    Persistence --> Application
    Runtime --> Application
    Application --> Evaluation
